			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I lay in the bed hardly able to move the sunlight is just starting to poor threw the window. My
<br />

<br />
eyes are heavy, I feel as if I have not opened them for years. I am in a strange place. I don't
<br />

<br />
remember were I am or what I am doing there. I lay there, the light growing brighter the walls
<br />

<br />
are white and clean and I can smell medicine in the air. I must be in some sort of infirmary. I
<br />

<br />
slowly sit up and wipe the sleep from my eyes. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Don't get up to quickly&quot; I hear a soft female voice speak. Who is there I ask not seeing
<br />

<br />
anyone. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;It is the lady Madeline I am watching over you child.&quot; My head is spinning and I lay back down.
<br />

<br />
Madeline comes over to my bedside and takes my hand and softly speaks &quot;My child what is
<br />

<br />
your name?&quot; 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Bewilder I can't answer I just look up at her not knowing what to say. Finally after a long
<br />

<br />
awkward silence the tears start to flow, a million questions are running threw my head. Who
<br />

<br />
am I? Where am I from? Who are my parents? How did I get here? Where is here? I try to
<br />

<br />
speak but have no voice. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I just lay in the bed confined in a prison of silence and confusion. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
It was two weeks later before I was able to get up and function with and sort of composure. It
<br />

<br />
was then that my training started. I was wandering the halls in the Paladin Guild there in
<br />

<br />
Felwithe and I ran right into a man, tall and handsome I step back and my mouth opened. I
<br />

<br />
hear in a deep voice &quot;Shut your mouth child.&quot; I am startled and I shut my mouth and stare up at
<br />

<br />
this man. I can hardly speak. &quot;What is your name?&quot; I am not sure what it was at that moment
<br />

<br />
but I spoke out and in a soft quite voice spoke Mechaela. &quot;My name is Jyleel.&quot; I bowed slightly.
<br />

<br />
He asked me why I looked so lost and I explained to him my problem and he suggested that I
<br />

<br />
meditate and find in my soul what it was that I was to be doing. Not quite sure what he was
<br />

<br />
talking about I followed him to the temple he sat me down and showed me how to pray. I sat
<br />

<br />
there for what seemed to be hours. I am asking over and over in my head &quot;What am I here for?&quot;
<br />

<br />
There was no answer. Nothing no Direction no Response. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I decided that I was not going to find answers in praying and that I would just go with the flow of
<br />

<br />
things till I did find some direction. So less then a month after I awoke I started my training with
<br />

<br />
Jyleel. At first I could hardly weald the sword he had given to me. The most I could do was a
<br />

<br />
couple swings. However I was very strong willed, I knew I could do it and would not accept
<br />

<br />
failure. I would practice until I had reached pure exhaustion and finally several weeks later Jyeel
<br />

<br />
told me it was time to go out on my own and try my hand and real life fighting. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Eagerly I left the security of felwithe into the woods of Greater Fay. Out in to this huge forest. I
<br />

<br />
started fighting and before I knew it I had heard word from Jyeel that I had moved up in rank. I
<br />

<br />
was so proud of my self in less then a month's time I made my way to the 4th rank. Then one
<br />

<br />
night running along the road I crossed paths with a very impressive individual whom I will not
<br />

<br />
name at this point. I had strayed from the road and was going the wrong way, when he hailed
<br />

<br />
me and offered to help. I was so happy to have met another Paladin; I accepted his help and
<br />

<br />
had a very long conversation with him. It was then that I realized that I truly was meant to be a
<br />

<br />
Paladin. This is also were another chapter of my live begins and I will finish it in the future.
<br />

<br />
 
<br />
