	<tr>
		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="9200"></a><b>Mechaela Morningstar</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Page<br /><img src="images/Ranks/swords/0sword.gif" alt="Page" title="Page" border="0" /><br /><br /><br />Joined: 03 Sep 2002<br />Posts: 11<br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9200&amp;sid=fd96919f5a5ba7bb1503e8ff236ec1b5#9200"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Sep 03, 2002 5:27 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9200&amp;sid=fd96919f5a5ba7bb1503e8ff236ec1b5"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Banegrivm that was his name.  I was young and he was the older more experienced human man.  My little elf ears were warm with emotion at the flatter he showed me the genuine care he seemed to express.  We talked for 5 hours that first night.  He told me he was the leader of one of the guild houses and that if I wanted he would welcome me into his family.  I was very happy to hear this good news and took the steps needed to join his cause.   A family I did not know what it meant to have a family but I was so happy to have found one.   
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
It was a couple days later that Trown a dwarven warrior whom comes to find out was a member of the family I was about to join approached me.  Trown told me that he had come with a gift for me from Banegrivm and that he would help me with my training if I wanted. The gift was a helmet one of enchantment that made me much stronger then the leather cap I had been wearing.  I took him up on his offer for help and we spent several weeks in training. We became closer and closer until one day we were in Crushbone fighting lego’s and I fell, twisting my ankle.  Before I knew it Trown was there on the ground checking my foot and then leaning up to kiss me.  I did not protest as I wanted to feel his lips touch mine.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Confused by the feelings that it awoke in me I pulled away and left the battle field I went back to Felwithe and to my room were I laid in bed wondering what I was thinking.   This family came to me offered me a haven and I like a silly girl fall for one of them and carelessly let my feelings show what must he think of me so eager to kiss I have most likely ruined any chanced I had with him. So there I was laying the in my room weeping for days before Trown convinced the head lady to allow him access to my room.   He woke me up my pillow still damp and asked me what the problem was.   He asked me if it was because he was a Dwarf and I a high elf.  I laughed a little at the thought of it.   The sight of us together must have been funny.  No it is not you I told him.   I just don’t want you to think ill of me being so willing to open myself to you.  He simply laid a finger across my lips and kissed my forehead. Then from that moment on we were inseparable we spent all our time together working up the ranks together and laughing loving and becoming the best of friends.   
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I was in my 15th rank the day we got the call from Banegrivm that our efforts were needed on a raid that the Guild was going on.   That is the day that I meet Qallain, Lamaridine, Marcelas, Parnhamien, and Cealyn.
<br />

<br />
 We were paired up into a group together Trown was not able to come he had more pressing matters come up with his family.   We went to battle that day together and we grew strong as group so much so that we continued to fight together whenever the opportunity arose.   Trown was gone all the time I hardly got to see him at all.  Which was ok because one of his friends Marcelas befriended me keeping me company any time my heart would start to become wiry from the lack of companionship I had grown so found of.  I heard word from Trown’s Brother Krown that Trown had grown ill and had asked that I not wait for him and instead that I would go on inspite of the things that we had planed and now knew would not happen. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I took the news very hard I was crying and in tears.  Marcelas was there though holding me and comforting me.  We grew very close it took longer but the feelings were much stronger then those felt with Trown.   I felt a little weird at times but things were much more natural between Marcelas and I.   Time passed and we grew older and I knew that I was happy.   Then the day came Marcelas took me out in to the ocean and to a secret room were he asked me to be his wife.   I was beaming at the thought could this really have happened.  Was I really in Love was I really going to be his wife?  I accepted and we started to plan things slowly not rushing things at all. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
It was not too far after that that those of us in the guild know as elders or officer or held office in the past Qallain, Lamaridine, Marcelas, Parnhamien, Cealyn, Flaural, Waylith, Kaylin, Tanla, and myself came together to start the Concordat Angelis.  Life was very good for Marcelas and I.  Then the day came when we went to his fathers House so that he could tell them of our up coming marriage.  It was that day that my world fell apart.   You see it was found that day as his father’s house that Marcelas and I were brother and sister.   I turned away from my family, friends.  I filled my time with hunting and working towards the Master levels that I desired.  Marcelas got married to a young wood elf and I was once again alone.  My heart ached and my age catching up to me.   I feared I would be a maiden my whole lives long.   
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
It was a few years later that I meet with a wizard a high elf by the name of Aldezworr.   I ran into him in West Commons as I invited him to join our guild the family I had isolated myself from for so long.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Again my life started to turn around and I became good friend with Aldezworr and we started hunting together when we could and spending time together.   But he was much older then me and his patients for my games were wearing thin.   He came around less and less and I grew more and more weary of my heart being broken again.    Then it happened I lost all the ability to maintain any sort of sanity I went off on a vacation a long one I have spent a great deal of time searching for myself trying to find were I belong.   I have come to terms with the life I have lived and am happy with who I am now.  Ready to start a new beginning in time. So when I asked myself what I was going to do I came to the one place that always came to mind as my home and that is here with the Concordat my true Family.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I am glad to be back and I look for Aldezworr often but as of yet I have nay seen him.  If you read this and see him around please tell him to leave a note for me with Indalis.  I have many things I must say to him. 
<br />

